SUMMARY
-------

  You may
    - Read and study the source code.
    - Run Akatsuki for yourself, including self-hosting it on your own
      machine or server.
    - Let members of your household and your friends use your self-hosted
      copy, as long as nobody pays anything for it.
    - Change the code for your own use.
    - Publish the source code of your changes (for example a public fork or
      a pull request), free of charge, under this same licence.
    - Compile Akatsuki and share the builds with anyone, free of charge,
      under this same licence (see section 3.4).
    - Contribute changes back to the project (see section 6).

  You may not
    - Use Akatsuki in or for a business, or for any commercial purpose.
    - Sell Akatsuki, or sell access to it.
    - Offer Akatsuki to others as a hosted or managed service.
    - Bundle Akatsuki, or any part of it, into a paid product.
    - Use Akatsuki to provide any service for a fee.
    - Sublicense Akatsuki, or relicense it under different terms.
    - Remove or change copyright, licence or attribution notices.
    - Use the Akatsuki name or logo for your own copy or product.

  Ask first (write to sami@samihindi.com)
    - Any of the "may not" uses above.
    - Use by an organisation of any kind, including non-profits, schools and
      public bodies.
    - Using a self-hosted copy for business email, including your own
      freelance or company mail.
    - Anything you are unsure about.


